witch from roughly that same time  period as a rather fortuitous  coincidence  although Hocus Pocus is clearly a movie  intended for the Halloween season it  actually hit theaters in July this means  that filming for the movie actually took  place around Christmas time which made  things a little tricky while summer  focused Focus was filmed at studios in  California some of the production did  actually take place in Salem  Massachusetts for authenticity  unfortunately when the crew traveled to  Salem people were starting to put up  their Christmas ornaments while holiday  cheer is great this was for the wrong  holiday this action had to be taken so  the filmmakers got out their checkbooks  and began approaching the locals add  dirt Tobias jelinek told e-news they  were having to pay them out block by  block to take down all their decorations  so we could get all the Halloween stuff  one of the scenes shot in La is the one  in which Max Dany and Alison celebrates  having just bested The Witches by  dancing around in a park outside the  school although there's nothing  particularly special about this short  scene internet sleuths have discovered  an unexpected cameo in the background as  it turns out this seemed was filmed at  the Old Warner Brothers Ranch in Burbank  the exact same location where the iconic  intro for friends were shot you can  clearly see the fountain that Joey  Rachel and the Gang play around then  behind Dany as she prances in the park  that's entertaining as Hocus Pocus is  the Journey of the screenplay behind the  movie is arguably even more interesting  at the 2018 Midsummer scream some of the  casts and crew members from Disney's fan  favorite Halloween flick reunited for  the 25th anniversary of the film's  release one of the members on the panel  was David kirschner a man credited with  creating the story kirschner explained  that it started as a bedtime story he  would tell to his daughters he  eventually wrote this as a short story  and it got published in Muppet magazine  then in 1986 the story was transformed  into a screenplay where it would sit in  limbo for eight years then kirschner  finally did sell the story to Disney he  reportedly brought in loads of Halloween  decorations including a giant bag chunk  full of candy corn so that the  executives smelled their childhood while  he gave his pitch  [ __ ] Banks a young boy from the late  1600s was cursed by winner Fred  Sanderson to live forever in the form of  a black cat  Bings is one of the high points of the  movie periodically cracking jokes at  Max's expense while watching over Dany  as though she was his own sister take  good care of Danny Max  you'll never know how precious she is  according to Humane Hollywood there were  several different cats that played Banks  throughout the movie and the handlers  chose which cat would appear in which  scene based on their skills and  personalities American Humane was  present throughout production ensuring  that no animals were harmed during  filming it's truly impressive what the  crew was able to accomplish with animal  actors  foreign  [Music]
 

